n, but they never contacted me about me after I contacted them numerous times in regards to the meditation claims. They had sent me secured messages about that situation, which expired and I no longer have access to. Fast forward to me filing a number of complaints with the better business bureau, they then retaliated by closing my accounts. After I questioned them, in regards to why the smaller charges that were done by the same company and provisional credit was provided they said it was merely a formality. The next day the reversed the credits, because they received another complaint from the XXXX. They pretty much told me they would not be returning my money, and there was nothing I could do about it and that they did not have to tell me how the investigation was conducted to validate their decision because it was an internal process. All in all, they denied XXXX claims by the same company. Why would I authorize more charges by a company that scammed me, after Wells Fargo had already denied my previous claim. Furthermore, as I was on the phone filing the claim, the company attempted to charge my account even more according to them. How can they justify that these charges were valid, the company 's stating they never charged me but my bank statements state otherwise. Wells Fargo had a duty to protect my money, which they failed miserably at. They claimed that a phone number was used to authorize the transactions, but ironically enough it was not the primary number listed on my account or the phone # they typically contact me on. This whole situation reeks of an internal fraud committed by Wells Fargo, they are moving like some dictators and taking money and closing accounts. I'm missing about XXXX, and I need assistance in getting my money back. Their representatives were rude, they attempt to bully me and pretty much taunt me about not getting my money back. There was XXXX representative who stated it was negligence on the bank 's part. I also spoke to the banker who opened my account ( XXXX XXXX XXXX, XXXX  branch ) who stated he's never seen anything like this before and that the bank should have put a freeze on the company 's access to my account. Wells Fargo violated my duty care of care, they put me in a bad financial situation and should be held liable.",Company has responded to the consumer and the CFPB and chooses not to provide a public response,WELLS FARGO & COMPANY,NY,11226,,Web,2024-10-01,Closed with explanation,Yes
