10318418,2024-10-02,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Incorrect information on your report,Account status incorrect,"XX/XX/XXXX Subject : Complaint Regarding Inaccurate Late Payment Entry on Credit Report Dear CFPB, I am writing to file a formal complaint against Equifax regarding an inaccurate late payment entry on my credit report that has not been resolved despite my attempts to rectify the issue. 

Account Information : Creditor 's Name : XXXX XXXX Account Number : XXXX Dates of Late Payments : XX/XX/XXXX, XX/XX/XXXX, XX/XX/XXXX and XX/XX/XXXX. 

Nature of Complaint : I submitted a dispute to Equifax disputing a late payment reported by XXXX XXXX. I referenced the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( 15 U.S. Code 1681i ) and the Truth in Lending Act ( TILA ) ( 15 U.S. Code 1637 ( b ) ) in my dispute, explaining that the reported late payment was inaccurate for the following reasons : Clerical error by XXXX XXXX  : It appears there was a clerical error in how XXXX XXXX  processed the payments. Despite making the payment on time, the account was incorrectly marked as overdue. I provided bank statements and payment receipts showing that the payments were processed. 
Evidence provided : I attached transaction records from my bank verifying that the payments were made on time, well before the 30-day delinquency threshold. I also included copies of emails from XXXX XXXX  confirming that no delinquency notice was sent to me. 
Despite providing this information and adhering to the dispute process within the Fair Credit Reporting Act, Equifax has failed to resolve this matter satisfactorily or remove the inaccurate late payment from my credit report. 

