10436096,2024-10-13,Credit reporting or other personal consumer reports,Credit reporting,Problem with a company's investigation into an existing problem,Their investigation did not fix an error on your report,"I am writing to file a formal complaint regarding the credit bureaus failure to properly investigate and validate a charge-off account listed on my credit report. I previously disputed the information related with XXXX XXXX because I believe it is inaccurate and was not substantiated by the original creditor. 

Issue Description : On XX/XX/year>, I disputed the accuracy of a charge-off account appearing on my credit report. 
In response to my dispute, the bureaus claimed the information had been validated with a billing statement from the creditor. 
However, a billing statement alone does not constitute proper validation of a debt, as it does not provide evidence from the original creditor that the account is legitimate, belongs to me, or that the debt was properly assigned. 
According to the Fair Credit Reporting Act ( FCRA ), the credit bureau is required to conduct a reasonable investigation and verify that the information is accurate by obtaining evidence from the creditor, such as contracts, original account agreements, or other relevant documentation. This was not done in my case. 

Why This is a Problem : A billing statement does not provide sufficient validation of a debt under the FCRA. 
The credit Bureaus have failed in its duty to investigate the legitimacy of the charge-off and has not provided any documentation proving the accuracy of the account beyond a basic billing statement. 
This failure has caused harm to my credit score and financial standing by allowing inaccurate and improperly substantiated information to remain on my credit report. 

Requested Resolution : I am requesting that the credit bureau be required to properly investigate this account by obtaining actual documentation from the original creditor that confirms the legitimacy of the debt, the amount owed, and my connection to the account. 
If they are unable to provide this documentation, I request that the charge-off account be removed from my credit report immediately. 
Additionally, I request that the CFPB investigate the credit bureaus violation of the FCRA regarding reasonable investigation procedures for disputed information. 

Thank you for your attention to this matter. I look forward to your prompt response and resolution of this issue.",,"EQUIFAX, INC.",GA,30252,Servicemember,Web,2024-10-13,Closed with non-monetary relief,Yes
