10614659,2024-10-29,"Payday loan, title loan, personal loan, or advance loan",Other advances of future income,Confusing or misleading advertising or marketing,,"I was approached by a company called XXXX XXXX after I filled out a form online to request information on going solar. I had not made any decision one way or the other, just wanted information about how things worked. Because I knew my property is in a direct location for collection of solar and I wanted to do my part in changing to green energy. I received a call from this company and was told that this was a great time to seek alternative energy sources as there is ( was ) government energy credits that help in the costs of installation of alternative energy sources of 30 %. So, this will make the project more affordable as the government would pay that portion of the costs. And they have engineers that will design the system such that I will not be paying more for my power in the way of a loan over what I was currently paying for power now. They asked me for access to the last 6 months of power bills. They said that they could put additional panels to make sure that there was enough surplus that it would likely give me a net +. In other words, that my energy cost of my loan would be less than the actual cost of the power I used. 
